{
  "id": "Compound::DB00300 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Tenofovir is implicated in the pathogenesis of multiple conditions, including Fanconi Syndrome, Osteomalacia, and Nephrosis Lower Nephron, all of which are linked to the binding of specific compounds to Slc22a6. These conditions are characterized by impaired renal function and altered ion transport, and the binding of Acetazolamide, Acetaminophen, and Cidofovir to Slc22a6 suggests a common mechanism involving the transport of ions across cellular membranes. The shared role of Slc22a6 in these pathways, coupled with the presence of an organonitrogen compound as a common ancestor, indicates that Tenofovir may influence Slc22a6 through a pathway involving the inhibition of enzyme activity or the modulation of ion transport. The integration of these findings highlights a potential role for Tenofovir in modulating Slc22a6 function, possibly through the indirect effects of compounds that bind to this transporter.",
